  "body": "Adds GitHub as an optional remote NEST location, preserving the local-dir NEST unchanged.\n\n## What\n- `src/mantle/nest/`: typed `NestTarget`, canonical manifest + transport seal, AESGCM Body-envelope (AAD-bound), materialize/hydrate lifecycle, exact-revision compare-and-swap, deterministic fake transport (hermetic tests), real stdlib-urllib transport, webhook normalization, outer orchestration runtime.\n- Recalibrated to GitHub's limits: build the whole tree locally, then **3 wire writes per checkpoint** (tree/commit/ref) \u2014 O(1) regardless of NEST size (GHNEST-4).\n- `nest` CLI family: inspect/connect/pull/push/sync/doctor/disconnect/install-template.\n- Inert SHA-pinned workflow templates (audit, heartbeat).\n- 20 executable GHNEST invariants with red cases; 6 new `TM-REMOTE-*` threat-model guarantees; 22 hermetic unit tests.\n- Docs: ADR, threat-model delta, operator guide, engineers \u00a712, README, and a Grimoire residency companion (ABODE law: local/cloud/github nesting forms).\n\n## Key boundary\nGitHub is OTHER, never SELF. Materialize \u2192 let the deterministic Body live offline \u2192 publish a secret-free, SELF-sealed checkpoint through exact-revision CAS. `body.json`/`genesis_key` never travel in plaintext.\n\nVerified: 168/168 invariants green, 22 hermetic tests pass, grimoire-tool verify passes, `git diff --check` clean.",
